              "estimatedMinutes": 25,
              "lesson": {
                "title": "What is Economics?",
                "introduction": "Economics studies how people and society choose to use scarce resources to satisfy unlimited wants.",
                "explanation": "Human wants are unlimited, but resources are scarce. This creates the central economic problem: scarcity. Because of scarcity, every choice involves a trade-off.\n\nOpportunity cost is the next best alternative you give up when you make a choice. If you spend N500 on a pen, its opportunity cost is what else you could have bought with N500.\n\nMicroeconomics studies individual units (households, firms). Macroeconomics studies the whole economy (inflation, unemployment, national income).",
                "keyPoints": [
                  "Wants are unlimited; resources are scarce.",
                  "Scarcity forces choices.",
                  "Opportunity cost = next best alternative given up.",
                  "Micro vs macro economics."
                ]
              },
